{
  "_comment": "Source of record for the laser ratchet section of the dashboard. Engine-side measurements, imported from the grootstebozewolf/jts fork at a pinned tip so this repo's Pages build stays on in-repo data (see .github/workflows/pages.yml). Never edit the numbers by hand without also moving the provenance tip.",

  "contract": {
    "expr": "t_laser ≤ 1.15 × t_chainsaw",
    "slack": 1.15,
    "scope": "measured per curve type (EXACT_CURVE_BIBLE §6, §7)"
  },

  "provenance": {
    "source_repo": "grootstebozewolf/jts",
    "branch": "feature/sfa-curve-rgr",
    "pr": 7,
    "tip": "c956b50d",
    "imported": "2026-08-22",
    "method": "nanoTime, median of 31 samples after 15 warmups (WARMUP=15, SAMPLES=31, NOISE=1.15), OpenJDK 21, single machine",
    "caveats": [
      "Hand-transcribed from javadoc and markdown tables in the fork. There is no JMH and no BenchmarkDotNet anywhere in the tree, and no captured run artifacts — every surefire report directory was searched and holds no perf output. Timings are printed to stdout at runtime and discarded.",
      "One measurement run, replicated byte-identically across all 13 jts-* worktrees (verified by md5) — not 13 independent runs. Treat as n=1.",
      "The chainsaw baseline is not stable between harness runs (Hausdorff two discs reads 29.212 ms in the red table and 15.5 ms in the current one; far discs 4.000 then 4.797). Ratios are comparable within a table, not across tables.",
      "A holding-gate count is not the ratchet. doc/LASER_RATCHET.md reports 'measured 11 (11 hold)' with no backing timing table; only the rows below have numbers."
    ]
  },

  "types": [
    { "name": "ExactCircularArc",   "implemented": true,  "measured": true,
      "note": "algorithm/exactcurve/ExactCircularArc.java — the only Exact* type that exists" },
    { "name": "ExactQuadraticBezier", "implemented": false, "measured": false,
      "note": "no source file; Bible §5 Year-2 order, first after the arc" },
    { "name": "ExactEllipticalArc", "implemented": false, "measured": false, "note": "no source file" },
    { "name": "ExactClothoid",      "implemented": false, "measured": false,
      "note": "no source file; ClothoidHaley lives in CompoundCurve, not as an Exact* type" },
    { "name": "ExactNurbsSegment",  "implemented": false, "measured": false,
      "note": "no source file; Bible §5 places single-span NURBS last" }
  ],

